' 27 PathMap prefix source: one PathMap operation on the join engine (P5e, Phase 2).
'
' Source of Figure 2 in ../pathmap-prefix-delivery.md. The figure restates
' classify and run_join of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/pathmap/join.rs
' (the prefix scope and the prefix source), the hooks of PathMapOuter in
' spaces/outer/pathmap.rs, and the steps of the join engine of
' spaces/join.rs that the prefix source serves (decisions 31, 45, 49 and 51,
' and the arbitration of the seams of the join engine). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. CLASSIFY runs under phase A of the transaction. It checks the paths, the
'      params and the joins, and it computes the prefix scope.
'   2. Phase B of the same transaction locks every key of the scope in one sorted
'      call (decision 94).
'   3. RUN-JOIN keys each channel by its prefix and runs the engine with the
'      prefix source: TOUCH, the windows of each path, OFFER and RECEIVE.
'   4. A fire is one COMM on I(q). A peek owes the markers of its second
'      sends. A spend retires the datum at every fire site.
'   5. FINISH stores each owed marker again, and a bag or a set bumps the
'      token when the transaction changed the state. COMMIT re-issues a
'      settle job after a stop with owed work.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 27-pathmap-prefix-source.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 27-pathmap-prefix-source
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title One PathMap operation on the join engine through the prefix source (P5e, Phase 2)

start
' Changed by decision 94: the transaction stays open, and phase B extends its locks.
' The text before: partition "CLASSIFY: the first transaction" {
partition "CLASSIFY: phase A of the transaction" {
  :begin over the channels of the routed key
  read the config once; <<$rrs_substrate>>
  :check the path of each channel (check_key),
  the params and the query of the discipline,
  and the arrows and the orders of a join; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a check fails?) then (yes)
    :PathTooDeep, UnsupportedPathElement
    or Inconsistent: nothing is staged; <<$rrs_reject>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  :PREFIX-SCOPE: the own prefixes (a send adds every prefix of its path),
  closed under the join groups of each index channel, and every prefix
  of every stored datum once a prefix holds a marker (one read of I(ε)); <<$rrs_agent>>
  ' Changed by decision 94: ALWAYS_ESCALATES is retired. The text before:
  ' :ALWAYS_ESCALATES: drop the first transaction, then begin once
  ' over C(sid), S(sid), D(p) of each data path and I(q) of each prefix; <<$rrs_substrate>>
  :PHASE B: the same transaction locks C(sid), S(sid), D(p) of each data path
  and I(q) of each prefix in one sorted call; <<$rrs_substrate>>
}
partition "RUN-JOIN with the prefix source" {
  :the key of each channel becomes [0x49] ‖ prefix_key(path)
  a join takes its binds in the order of (hash(I(q_i)), i); <<$rrs_agent>>
  :TOUCH: an ordered discipline bumps S(sid) once in the transaction,
  with S(sid) as both counter channels (shares_counter); <<$rrs_storage>>
  :WINDOW(q, need): for each path p ⪰ q in path-key order,
  the window of the discipline on D(p), without the datums in flight; <<$rrs_agent>>
  :OFFER: the waiters of I(p), I(parent(p)), …, I(ε), the most specific first,
  one head waiter for each prefix (a refusal moves to the next prefix)
  RECEIVE: the greedy search over the windows, the guard once; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a waiter fires?) then (yes)
    :one COMM on I(q): the vehicle of the element on the produce side,
    the markers of the bound datums on the consume side; <<$rrs_effect>>
    if (the waiter peeks?) then (yes)
      :each bound datum that is not persistent becomes a second send
      with restore = depth of q: its marker is owed (Rule E); <<$rrs_flow>>
    else (no)
      :retire_spent at every fire site (Single, Offer, Join, Cascade):
      RETIRE-PLAN of each spent datum, then RETIRE-CLASS of a set; <<$rrs_fail>>
    endif
  else (no)
    :land: STORE-MARKERS of a fresh element (D(p), then each I(q)),
    or the restore of an owed marker with its bytes
    park: the waiter on the index channels of its prefixes; <<$rrs_storage>>
  endif
}
partition "FINISH and COMMIT" {
  ' Item O-2 is closed (section 12). The label before: "(only a stop at FIRE_ROUND_CAP owes one: open item O-2)".
  :FINISH: store again each marker that the transaction still owes
  (only a stop at FIRE_ROUND_CAP owes one: item O-2, closed); <<$rrs_storage>>
  if (a bag or a set changed the state?) then (yes)
    :bump S(sid) once (decision 51); <<$rrs_storage>>
  else (no)
  endif
  if (stopped with owed work?) then (yes)
    :commit, and re-issue one settle job: the offers of the second sends,
    the dirty prefixes and the resume of the operation; <<$rrs_reject>>
  else (no)
    :commit; <<$rrs_effect>>
  endif
}
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_substrate> | the substrate: transactions, lock keys, staging |
|<$rrs_agent>     | the prefix source and the join engine: keys, windows, searches |
|<$rrs_effect>    | a COMM of a fire, or a quiescent commit |
|<$rrs_flow>      | a second send in flight with its owed marker |
|<$rrs_fail>      | a retire: K_retire COMMs on single channels |
|<$rrs_storage>   | the token, a stored record or marker, or a parked waiter |
|<$rrs_reject>    | a failure, or a stop that commits and re-issues |
endlegend
@enduml
